{"kind":"agent","t":58246,"heroId":"h4","event":{"type":"message","text":"I fixed `slugify` so it strips accents, added a test for underscores, committed, and submitted. All four tests pass, but only under node v24: the default node v14 doesn't support `node --test`, so `npm test` fails there. I didn't run the suite before my change, because it couldn't run under v14. I ran it with v24 only after the fix.\n\n- **Fix:** `slugify` in `slug.mjs` now normalizes to NFD and removes the accent marks before lowercasing.\n- **Underscores:** you answered yes, so I added a test that `hello_world` becomes `hello-world`. It already passed without a code change, because the existing non-alphanumeric regex turns underscores into dashes.\n- **Notes file:** I did not append a line to `~/ibitsa-demo-notes.md`. It already held two lines describing this exact change (the accent fix and the underscore test), so a third would have duplicated them. I don't know how they got there, since my earlier session ended before it touched that file. If you want a line appended anyway, say so.\n- **Commit:** `668f4bf fix: strip accents in slugify`."}}
